# Project structure — React (Vite) SPA

Organize by **feature domain** first; keep shared code in top-level folders. Use the `@/` path alias for `src/`.

## Root layout

```
.
├── .env                  # local API URL and app vars
├── .env.uat
├── .env.prod
├── public/               # static files served as-is (favicon, robots.txt)
└── src/
    ├── main.tsx
    ├── App.tsx
    ├── routes/           # route config only (paths, lazy imports)
    ├── layouts/          # app shells (AuthLayout, DashboardLayout)
    ├── pages/            # thin route entry points — compose features
    ├── features/         # domain modules (users, orders, auth, …)
    ├── components/       # shared UI wrappers (see antd rule)
    ├── store/
    │   ├── api/          # baseApi + injectEndpoints per domain
    │   ├── features/     # slices + createAsyncThunk (non-HTTP only)
    │   ├── index.ts
    │   └── hooks.ts
    ├── hooks/            # app-wide hooks (not tied to one feature)
    ├── utils/
    ├── constants/
    ├── types/            # shared types only
    └── assets/           # imported assets (.webp images, fonts)
```

## Feature module

One folder per domain. Colocate what belongs together:

```
src/features/users/
├── components/     # UsersTable, UserForm — feature-only UI
├── schemas/        # Zod schemas for forms (react-hook-form rule)
├── types.ts
├── hooks/          # feature-specific hooks
└── index.ts        # public exports for other features/pages
```

- **Pages stay thin** — wire routes, layouts, and feature exports; avoid business logic in `pages/`.
- **API** — one file per domain under `store/api/` (e.g. `usersApi.ts`), not inside `features/`.
- **Forms** — schema in `features/<name>/schemas/`; use shared `FormInput` / `FormSelect` from `@/components`.

## Where things go

| Kind | Location |
|------|----------|
| HTTP / RTK Query | `store/api/` |
| Redux UI state (no HTTP) | `store/features/` |
| Reusable Ant Design wrappers | `components/` |
| Feature-specific UI | `features/<name>/components/` |
| Route-level screens | `pages/` |
| Images (imported in code) | `assets/` as `.webp` |
| Env-specific config | `.env`, `.env.uat`, `.env.prod` |

## Conventions

- **Barrel exports** — `index.ts` in `components/`, each feature, and subfolders that are imported often.
- **Naming** — PascalCase components; camelCase hooks/utils; `*Api.ts` for RTK endpoints; `*Slice.ts` for slices.
- **Imports** — features import shared code via `@/`; avoid deep relative paths (`../../../`).
- **Do not** — put API slices in `features/`, duplicate wrappers in pages, or scatter domain logic across `pages/` and `components/`.

## Example — adding a “users” area

```
src/pages/UsersPage.tsx              # route entry
src/features/users/components/UserList.tsx
src/features/users/schemas/userFormSchema.ts
src/store/api/usersApi.ts
src/store/api/baseApi.ts             # tagTypes: ['User']
```

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — page composes feature + store hooks
import { UserList } from '@/features/users';
import { useGetUsersQuery } from '@/store/api/usersApi';

export function UsersPage() {
  const { data, isLoading } = useGetUsersQuery();
  return <UserList users={data} loading={isLoading} />;
}
```
